Developer notes for Shattered-Maps, the world-map work (the `docs/{service}/{feature}.md` convention in docs/claude/work-item-workflow.md). The plan that builds it is .ai-plans/active/2026-11-05_copilot-ai-training-sibling-to-autopilot/ (Phase 19 on). schema.md is the model's reference: levels, the identity and link-evidence rules (D12), merge and split, the baseline rule (D13), the strict reader, the exporters. import-azah.md describes the community-map import (the columns read, the zone rules, the newest-wins rule, the real counts). app.md is the viewer: how to run it, the neutral viewer and candidate review (Phase 23), the classic editor kept at #/legacy. user-guide.md is the end-user page (zoom levels, reading gaps and off-page links, the baseline, reviewing candidates). builder-export.md is the export of an area or subzone to a Merc .are file for MUD Builder (Phase 24): the field mapping, the room number rule, what the file leaves out, why the page never calls the Builder. Later pages (the server API) are added by the phase that delivers them.

Unlike docs/copilot this is production-bound material: it describes `services/shattered-maps-core`, which carries no Copilot marker. The data Copilot walks into the map is local-only; the model and the viewer are not. The end-user guide for the map surfaces is docs/shattered-maps/user-guide.md.

Codenames only in examples and fixtures; no real character names (docs/standards/data-classification.md).

world-map-api.md describes the C# side that serves the map (Phase 25 on): GET /api/health, the local-only candidate routes, the CopilotLocal build gate and how to verify the production shape (Server/scripts/verify-prod-output.mjs in the DSL repo). The candidate files are NOT under wwwroot: the local compose file mounts Copilot private folder read-only (amendment A35).
The publisher (services/shattered-maps-core/scripts/publish-audited.mjs) and the audited routes are in world-map-api.md; the audited file comes from the Mapper, the slices go into the DSL repo wwwroot/data/world-map, and the owner commits and deploys.
surfaces.md lists the places that show the map (the Mapper, the C# page /maps/world-v2, later the game-client pane and the mobile screen) and how the shared renderer reaches the C# site as one generated script (scripts/publish-map-renderer.mjs).
surfaces.md now also covers the web game-client map pane (apps/game-client features/worldmap + WorldMapPane); docs/game-client.md has a short Right sidebar section that points to it.

verification.md is how Azah's candidates are checked against the owner's game logs (the tracer, the layer comparison, the real numbers from the 2026 logs and the lessons for Copilot's first use). Azah mapped the DSL only: every command there takes --world dsl and refuses another world.

worlds.md is the rule that keeps the DSL's map and the Simulacrum's apart (two worlds, the Simulacrum local only, the world chosen by the connection and never by a production picker) and how each is built.

map-backup.md (Phase 44) is the player's cloud backup of explored and added room ids on their account: the routes, the document shape and caps, why ids only, and that it runs only on the Sync now press. Its C# half lives in the DSL repo (Server.Dsl/Maps/MapVisitSync.cs); change the shape or a cap in both places and in the client (features/worldmap/sync/backup.ts) together.

continent-layout.md (Phases 45-46) is the continent layout (spec format, the compass relations, room-count versus extent sizing, the owner's Arkane geography) and the tangled-link / maze drawing (diamond, hourglass, hexagons) with the commands to rebuild the slices.
terrain.md (2026-11-14) is the room terrain: the palette, mining the sector out of the game's GMCP room_data logs (mine-terrain.mjs), what the first run gave (33% of the DSL rooms) and where it is shown. surfaces.md says the C# page replaced the beta map (301 from /maps/world-map, linked under Tools).
